INSERT INTO "questions" VALUES(4905,374,'BG10.2',10,2,1,1,'match_pairs','beginner','Match the Sanskrit words to their English meanings','Connect each Sanskrit word from the verse with its correct meaning:',NULL,'{"words": ["Commentary", "sages", "it", "their"], "meanings": ["is very difficult for them to know Me.Sarvasah In every way -- not only am I the source of all the gods and the sages but also their efficient cause", "Prabhavam Origin. It may also mean great lordly power.Maharshis great sages like Bhrigu.As I am the source of all these gods", "and living beings", "inner ruler and the dispenser or ordainer and the guide of their intellect"]}','{"Commentary": "Prabhavam Origin. It may also mean great lordly power.Maharshis great sages like Bhrigu.As I am the source of all these gods", "sages": "and living beings", "it": "is very difficult for them to know Me.Sarvasah In every way -- not only am I the source of all the gods and the sages but also their efficient cause", "their": "inner ruler and the dispenser or ordainer and the guide of their intellect"}','In verse BG10.2, these core words establish the setting and emotional tension of the dialogue.','Focus on the root meanings used in classical Sanskrit.',15);
INSERT INTO "questions" VALUES(4906,374,'BG10.2',10,2,1,2,'mcq_vocab','beginner','Select the correct meaning','What does the Sanskrit word "Commentary" mean in this verse?','Commentary','["Prabhavam Origin. It may also mean great lordly power.Maharshis great sages like Bhrigu.As I am the source of all these gods", "is very difficult for them to know Me.Sarvasah In every way -- not only am I the source of all the gods and the sages but also their efficient cause", "and living beings", "inner ruler and the dispenser or ordainer and the guide of their intellect"]','"Prabhavam Origin. It may also mean great lordly power.Maharshis great sages like Bhrigu.As I am the source of all these gods"','"Commentary" translates directly to "Prabhavam Origin. It may also mean great lordly power.Maharshis great sages like Bhrigu.As I am the source of all these gods" in the context of this shloka.','Break down the compound word or root prefix.',10);
INSERT INTO "questions" VALUES(4907,374,'BG10.2',10,2,1,3,'mcq_vocab','beginner','Select the correct meaning','What is the meaning of "sages"?','sages','["and living beings", "Prabhavam Origin. It may also mean great lordly power.Maharshis great sages like Bhrigu.As I am the source of all these gods", "is very difficult for them to know Me.Sarvasah In every way -- not only am I the source of all the gods and the sages but also their efficient cause", "inner ruler and the dispenser or ordainer and the guide of their intellect"]','"and living beings"','"sages" means "and living beings", a crucial term in verse BG10.2.','Recall the verse breakdown.',10);
INSERT INTO "questions" VALUES(4908,374,'BG10.2',10,2,1,4,'mcq_reverse_vocab','intermediate','Identify the Sanskrit word','Which Sanskrit word from this verse means: "is very difficult for them to know Me.Sarvasah In every way -- not only am I the source of all the gods and the sages but also their efficient cause"?',NULL,'["Commentary", "sages", "it", "their"]','"it"','The term "it" corresponds directly to "is very difficult for them to know Me.Sarvasah In every way -- not only am I the source of all the gods and the sages but also their efficient cause".','Check the word roots.',10);
