INSERT INTO "questions" VALUES(5547,423,'BG11.9',11,9,2,7,'word_order','advanced','Tap the words in the correct sequence to reconstruct the shloka','Reconstruct this line in its sacred order:','एवमुक्त्वा ततो राजन्महायोगेश्वरो हरिः |','["राजन्महायोगेश्वरो", "एवमुक्त्वा", "ततो", "|", "हरिः"]','["एवमुक्त्वा", "ततो", "राजन्महायोगेश्वरो", "हरिः", "|"]','Correct sequence: एवमुक्त्वा ततो राजन्महायोगेश्वरो हरिः |. Word-order recitation strengthens memory and concentration.','Start with the first word of the chapter or verse.',20);
INSERT INTO "questions" VALUES(5548,423,'BG11.9',11,9,3,8,'speaker_context','beginner','Identify the speaker of this verse','Who is the speaker in verse BG11.9?','सञ्जय उवाच |','["Bhagavan Sri Krishna", "King Dhritarashtra", "Arjuna", "Sanjaya"]','"Sanjaya"','This verse is spoken by Sanjaya. Understanding who is speaking reveals their mindset, doubts, and spiritual readiness.','Look at the introductory phrase (uvācha) preceding the shloka.',10);
INSERT INTO "questions" VALUES(5549,423,'BG11.9',11,9,3,9,'translation_mcq','intermediate','Select the most accurate translation of this shloka','Which translation accurately expresses verse BG11.9?',NULL,'["Sanjaya recounted the ancient lineages of the Kuru dynasty and their celestial origins.", "The kings gathered to celebrate their victory and distribute royal riches among the priests.", "11.9 Sanjaya said  Having thus spoken, O king, the great Lord of Yoga, hari (Krishna), showed to Arjuna His supreme form as the Lord.", "Arjuna laid down his bow and arrows, requesting Krishna to lead the armies away from battle."]','"11.9 Sanjaya said  Having thus spoken, O king, the great Lord of Yoga, hari (Krishna), showed to Arjuna His supreme form as the Lord."','Accurate translation: "11.9 Sanjaya said  Having thus spoken, O king, the great Lord of Yoga, hari (Krishna), showed to Arjuna His supreme form as the Lord.".','Identify the key actors and actions described in the Sanskrit words.',15);
INSERT INTO "questions" VALUES(5550,423,'BG11.9',11,9,3,10,'true_false','beginner','Evaluate the statement as True or False','True or False: "In verse BG11.9, Sanjaya is expressing an inquiry or observation regarding the battlefield."',NULL,'["True", "False"]','"True"','True. This shloka directly conveys Sanjaya''s focus and psychological state at this point of the epic.','Reflect on who spoke and the setting.',10);
INSERT INTO "questions" VALUES(5551,423,'BG11.9',11,9,4,11,'philosophical_insight','intermediate','Select the deepest philosophical interpretation','What central spiritual wisdom does BG 11.9 reveal for self-mastery?',NULL,'["Cultivating equanimity, selfless duty (Nishkama Karma), and dedication of all actions to the Supreme.", "Rejecting work and retiring completely from society.", "Pursuing personal ambition while disregarding moral consequences.", "Blaming external circumstances for one''s emotional state."]','"Cultivating equanimity, selfless duty (Nishkama Karma), and dedication of all actions to the Supreme."','The Gita repeatedly emphasizes performing one''s prescribed duties without obsessive craving for the fruits.','Look for the answer highlighting inner consciousness and detachment over superficial attachment.',20);
