INSERT INTO "questions" VALUES(5555,424,'BG11.10',11,10,1,1,'match_pairs','beginner','Match the Sanskrit words to their English meanings','Connect each Sanskrit word from the verse with its correct meaning:',NULL,'{"words": ["अनेकवक्त्रनयनम्", "अनेकाद्भुतदर्शनम्", "अनेकदिव्याभरणम्", "दिव्यानेकोद्यतायुधम्"], "meanings": ["with numerous wonderful sights", "with numerous divine weapons uplifted.Commentary Countless faces appeared there. Arjuna looked at this Cosmic Form in all its magnificence. He saw the Lord everywhere and in everything. The whole manifestation appeared as one gigantic body of the Lord. He saw the Lord as the allinall", "with numerous mouthsand eyes", "with numerous divine ornaments"]}','{"अनेकवक्त्रनयनम्": "with numerous mouthsand eyes", "अनेकाद्भुतदर्शनम्": "with numerous wonderful sights", "अनेकदिव्याभरणम्": "with numerous divine ornaments", "दिव्यानेकोद्यतायुधम्": "with numerous divine weapons uplifted.Commentary Countless faces appeared there. Arjuna looked at this Cosmic Form in all its magnificence. He saw the Lord everywhere and in everything. The whole manifestation appeared as one gigantic body of the Lord. He saw the Lord as the allinall"}','In verse BG11.10, these core words establish the setting and emotional tension of the dialogue.','Focus on the root meanings used in classical Sanskrit.',15);
INSERT INTO "questions" VALUES(5556,424,'BG11.10',11,10,1,2,'mcq_vocab','beginner','Select the correct meaning','What does the Sanskrit word "अनेकवक्त्रनयनम्" mean in this verse?','अनेकवक्त्रनयनम्','["with numerous divine ornaments", "with numerous divine weapons uplifted.Commentary Countless faces appeared there. Arjuna looked at this Cosmic Form in all its magnificence. He saw the Lord everywhere and in everything. The whole manifestation appeared as one gigantic body of the Lord. He saw the Lord as the allinall", "with numerous wonderful sights", "with numerous mouthsand eyes"]','"with numerous mouthsand eyes"','"अनेकवक्त्रनयनम्" translates directly to "with numerous mouthsand eyes" in the context of this shloka.','Break down the compound word or root prefix.',10);
INSERT INTO "questions" VALUES(5557,424,'BG11.10',11,10,1,3,'mcq_vocab','beginner','Select the correct meaning','What is the meaning of "अनेकाद्भुतदर्शनम्"?','अनेकाद्भुतदर्शनम्','["with numerous mouthsand eyes", "with numerous divine ornaments", "with numerous divine weapons uplifted.Commentary Countless faces appeared there. Arjuna looked at this Cosmic Form in all its magnificence. He saw the Lord everywhere and in everything. The whole manifestation appeared as one gigantic body of the Lord. He saw the Lord as the allinall", "with numerous wonderful sights"]','"with numerous wonderful sights"','"अनेकाद्भुतदर्शनम्" means "with numerous wonderful sights", a crucial term in verse BG11.10.','Recall the verse breakdown.',10);
INSERT INTO "questions" VALUES(5558,424,'BG11.10',11,10,1,4,'mcq_reverse_vocab','intermediate','Identify the Sanskrit word','Which Sanskrit word from this verse means: "with numerous divine ornaments"?',NULL,'["अनेकवक्त्रनयनम्", "अनेकदिव्याभरणम्", "दिव्यानेकोद्यतायुधम्", "अनेकाद्भुतदर्शनम्"]','"अनेकदिव्याभरणम्"','The term "अनेकदिव्याभरणम्" corresponds directly to "with numerous divine ornaments".','Check the word roots.',10);
