kṣudraṃ hṛdayadaurbalyaṃ tyaktvottiṣṭha parantapa ||2-3||','क्लैब्यम्—impotence; मा—स्म गमः do not get; पार्थ—O Partha; न—not; एतत्—this; त्वयि—in thee; उपपद्यते—is fitting; क्षुद्रम्—mean; हृदयदौर्बल्यम्—weakness of the heart; त्यक्त्वा—having abandoned; उत्तिष्ठ—stand up; परन्तप—O scorcher of the foes.No commentary','2.3 Yield not to impotence, O Arjuna, son of Pritha. It does not befit thee. Cast off this mean weakness of the heart! Stand up, O scorcher of the foes!','','Narrator / Sanjaya',NULL,'Vedic Scriptures API: Swami Sivananda','Yield not to impotence, O Arjuna, son of Pritha. It does not befit thee. Cast off this mean weakness of the heart! Stand up, O scorcher of the foes! Chapter 2 explores the self, duty, and steady wisdom. Read with nearby verses, this line connects its immediate message to the dialogue''s wider teaching.');
