इषुभिः प्रतियोत्स्यामि पूजार्हावरिसूदन ||२-४||','arjuna uvāca .
kathaṃ bhīṣmamahaṃ saṅkhye droṇaṃ ca madhusūdana .
iṣubhiḥ pratiyotsyāmi pūjārhāvarisūdana ||2-4||','कथम्—how; भीष्मम्—Bhishma; अहम्—I; संख्ये—in battle; द्रोणम्—Drona; च—and; मधुसूदन—O Madhusudana; इषुभिः—with arrows; प्रतियोत्स्यामि—shall fight; पूजार्हौ—worthy to be worshipped; अरिसूदन—O destroyer of enemies.No commentary','2.4 Arjuna said  How, O Madhusudana, shall I fight in battle with arrows against Bhishma and Drona, who are fit to be worshipped, O destroyer of enemies?','','Arjuna',NULL,'Vedic Scriptures API: Swami Sivananda','Arjuna said How, O Madhusudana, shall I fight in battle with arrows against Bhishma and Drona, who are fit to be worshipped, O destroyer of enemies? Chapter 2 explores the self, duty, and steady wisdom. Read with nearby verses, this line connects its immediate message to the dialogue''s wider teaching.');
